WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.837
A Boolean mask is an array of true and false values created by testing a condition.

00:00:05.837 --> 00:00:11.242
Suppose we have sales values and compare the array with one hundred.

00:00:11.242 --> 00:00:16.827
NumPy returns true for values above one hundred and false for the others.

00:00:17.471 --> 00:00:21.753
We can then use that Boolean mask to keep only the matching values.

00:00:21.753 --> 00:00:29.123
This is a very powerful pattern because it lets us filter data without writing an if statement for every element.

00:00:29.123 --> 00:00:32.043
You will see the same idea again in Pandas.

00:00:32.043 --> 00:00:40.003
In real analysis, Boolean masks are useful for finding high-value transactions, unusual sensor readings,

00:00:40.003 --> 00:00:44.601
ages within a certain range, or any other values that meet a condition.
